id: pm-github-2e38
title: Preview exact GitHub label migration impacts
description: "Plan provider label renames and explicit consolidations across stored tags, declared import filters and local mappings, with exact identity evidence, bounded output and stale-plan refusal."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: labels,migration,planning
created_at: "2026-10-27T06:17:55.248Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T13:21:36.677Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Same display intent never merges labels by inference; 1000 items yield complete counts and bounded affected rows; stale provider label IDs invalidate application plans; typed SDK and CLI, strict boundaries, non-git read-only validation and seeded state properties."
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T06:18:14.443Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against installed core SDK bulk mutations and sibling pm-linear/pm-jira docs. Core edits local tags; github identity explores competing ownership; Linear negotiates team schema. None previews a GitHub label policy across exact provider IDs, stored tag occurrences, declared import filters and export mappings. Scope: read-only plans plus fresh revalidation; no new importer, exporter, sync writer, journal, resolver or remote mutation. Existing importer stores label names rather than label IDs, so name matches are reported as unverified occurrences requiring an explicit choice, never inferred consolidation. Acceptance covers distinct same-intent IDs, complete 1000-item counts with bounded rows, stale IDs/revisions, strict input/output schemas, real non-git SDK state and packed consumers. Registry reports CLI 2026.10.27; repo pin remains 2026.10.20 per queue rule."
  "2026-10-27T06:29:10.429Z",codex-agent,"Implementation adds a read-only typed planner and github labels plan command. Exact node IDs and expected provider names select identities; SDK toImportTags finds native normalized occurrences without merging provider IDs. Choices cover tag/filter/mapping policy; complete counts accompany bounded rows. Revalidation reads fresh catalogs and current SDK revisions rather than replaying saved mutations. The 1000-item read-only non-git fixture passes. Targeted boundary tests cover sparse/extreme inputs, same-intent IDs, stale deleted/recreated labels and revision changes; seeded 500-sequence model checks are being completed. No stateful writer/journal/import/export/sync path is introduced."
  "2026-10-27T06:34:03.464Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: independently replacing SDK-native tag conversion with exact provider spelling, disabling current approval/revision comparison, and removing the row cap each makes its targeted regression fail (exit 1). Restoring the code passes. Targeted tests: 7/7 including 500 seeded operation sequences; targeted planner coverage is 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Public non-git read-only tracker at main 2b71f73: 155 items scanned, 12 provider labels, one affected item/tag and two declared policy examples (one filter, one mapping), 3 rows, 1078 JSON bytes; byte identity preserved. Isolated packed installation acceptance is in progress."
  "2026-10-27T06:36:05.537Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm linked-test execution completed: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/labels.test.ts passed 7/7, including all 500 seeded sequences (89.6 seconds). Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment retains the measured result without changing policy. Three independent behavioral reversions failed as expected, then were restored. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstring checks pass; full npm/Bun release evidence will come from unchanged CI gates."
  "2026-10-27T06:58:57.868Z",codex-agent,"PR 188 is ready for review. All five packed consumers pass on CLI 2026.10.26: project-local, npx, native Bun/bunx, npm-global and Bun-global; each verifies JSON, TOON, current approval and byte-identical public tracker source. Public snapshot remains 155 items, 12 labels, one affected item/tag and two explicitly declared policies, 3 rows and 1078 JSON bytes. Added a passing bounded-provenance regression: oversized or malformed foreign references cannot fail an otherwise valid affected item. Reverting that guard alone fails the test (exit 1). Full unchanged npm/Bun CI gates are running; final-head run URLs and exact counts are maintained in the PR. Automated reviews are unavailable or skipped and are not approvals. No CLI/SDK defect was identified; installation-harness corrections preserved actual package layouts rather than relocating dependencies."
  "2026-10-27T08:08:18.534Z",codex-agent,"Final-head run 40464566061 passed all four full npm/Bun release gates (1526 tests each, exact 100/100/100/100 across 22 modules) and the Node 26 native Bun suite (1526 tests across 57 files). Node 22 native Bun failed only the 1000-item fixture, whose SDK read contained 999 items; its other seven feature regressions, including all 500 model sequences, passed. The fixture used a random SDK seed ID and a synthetic numeric ID range that can overlap and overwrite that seed. Correcting the fixture to use disjoint IDs and certifying its source count through the SDK before the read-only preview. No production planner mutation is involved."
  "2026-10-27T08:11:50.180Z",codex-agent,"Deterministic collision proof confirms fixture defect: force the seed ID into the old numeric clone range and the source SDK count becomes 999; reverting only the disjoint clone namespace fails under both Node and Bun (exit 1). Fixed fixture uses an exact seed ID, descendants in a separate namespace, and a certified SDK source count of 1000 before preview. The corrected focused test passes under Node, Bun 1.3.5 and CI-matching Bun 1.3.14. Production labels.ts and the packed runtime surface are unchanged. Re-running the complete CI matrix after the fixture correction; all thresholds and dependency pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T10:17:20.283Z",codex-agent,"Re-review blocking finding accepted. General rule: provider label names follow GitHub's case-insensitive matching everywhere they are compared or combined; opaque node IDs, local mapping keys and exact catalog revision bindings remain exact. Package-wide audit found the missing matches in label-plan filters and mapping destinations, plus case-sensitive deduplication in applyLabelMap (including no-map exports), issue-form contract labels and form/export label composition. REST request emission will use the same provider-name rule. Raw import/refresh label payloads remain governed by SDK-native tag normalization; form question labels and configured status names are separate domains. origin/main is not ahead (0 commits behind), so no merge is needed. No additional actionable non-blocking findings were supplied or published in PR review comments; all newly found class instances will be covered."
  "2026-10-27T10:35:21.684Z",codex-agent,"Focused class regressions pass: all eight ASCII case spellings of bug across rename and consolidation; SDK and registered CLI JSON/TOON reports; off-page unresolved policy choices; exact node IDs and expected-name revision bindings; first-spelling preservation; 500 export/form case permutations; form/export composition; direct POST and PATCH payload normalization. Existing 500 SDK state sequences now replay mixed-case policy inputs with an independent presence-based reference model. Full feature-file coverage is still running on the loaded host. Operational test runners now explicitly use at most two workers. Pinned pm 2026.10.20 refuses linked-test metadata edits through --update-index/--set-json because the declared peer floor cannot safely refuse item format 2; normal files/comments/add operations work, so existing test entries and pins are preserved and a separate focused entry has timeout 600."
  "2026-10-27T10:41:39.819Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: independently restoring case-sensitive filter matching, mapping destinations, mapped/unmapped export deduplication, issue-form contract labels, form/export composition, PATCH labels, POST labels, rename collisions, or the shared name key makes its focused regression fail (all nine exit 1). Removing the two-worker cap independently fails its guard test (exit 1). Every changed file was restored byte-for-byte after each proof. Full focused feature run passed 11/11, including 500 mixed-case SDK state sequences plus 500 generated export/form permutations; planner and shared-name helper both have exact 100/100/100/100 targeted coverage. Pinned pm linked-test run passed the three provider-name class tests. Catalog revision bindings, opaque IDs and local mapping keys remain exact by explicit adversarial assertions."
  "2026-10-27T10:44:00.100Z",codex-agent,"Restored-code follow-up checks passed: legacy export and worker-cap regressions 9/9; native Bun 1.3.14 class regressions 3/3; typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstrings pass. The shared provider-name helper is used at every comparison/combination site found in the package audit. No tests were removed or weakened. Full gates remain CI evidence with explicit --test-concurrency=2; native Bun files run serially. Final-head gate counts and fresh mixed-case packed consumer receipts will be recorded in PR 188."
  "2026-10-27T11:09:30.696Z",codex-agent,"Current review-fix source is 4930a98. Full CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/40491011369 has all four npm/Bun Node 22/26 jobs queued with no assigned runners; no current-head full gate has passed or failed. Queue rules cap post-push waiting at 30 minutes, so pending checks must remain explicit rather than being reported as acceptance. A documentation-only receipt commit will preserve this status; PR 188 records its final-head run and exact pending jobs. Exact review-fix packed acceptance passed all five install modes on CLI 2026.10.26 and Bun 1.3.14: public tracker 155 items, 12 labels, one affected item/tag plus one declared filter and one mapping, 3 rows and 1078 JSON bytes; every source copy remained byte-identical. Duplication check passed across 23 authored modules with zero duplicated lines. No additional source changes or full local suites are needed while CI is queued."
  "2026-10-27T11:34:07.124Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 finding accepted. General rule: previews and read-back comparisons must call the same exported conversion as the importer write path, never a second normalization. The importer joins tag values as CSV before SDK parsing, whereas the planner used the SDK array branch and missed embedded commas. Audit covers preparation, atomic create/update/link-only writes, import validation/read-back, refresh deltas, SDK/CLI JSON/TOON and packed consumers. Provider policy names retain GitHub name semantics; opaque IDs and exact catalog bindings remain exact. Merged the one origin/main release-version commit cleanly before edits. No additional actionable non-blocking review comments were published."
  "2026-10-27T11:56:34.375Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class audit completed across the flat package source (there is no src directory). One exported importer-owned githubLabelsToTags joins the writer CSV representation and calls the SDK string tag parser. Preparation, plain and atomic create/update/link-only writes, provenance validation, refresh comparison/emission and label-plan source/stored/destination tags now share it. Provider label policy names, exact node IDs, repository locators and project field identities are different domains and keep their existing domain-specific producers/parsers. CSV SDK/CLI JSON/TOON regressions pass, including zero-tag destinations, Unicode expansion and legacy SDK array-producer data. Revert proof: independently reverting the shared converter, source expansion, stored normalization, complete destination expansion, preparation, refresh comparison, refresh delta emission, native mutation paths or provenance validation fails its regression (all nine exit 1); every production file was restored byte-for-byte. No tests were removed or weakened. Local strict health has clean history/integrity but reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew between pinned 2026.10.20 and 2026.10.27; pins remain unchanged, and complete gates are CI evidence."
  "2026-10-27T12:14:56.742Z",codex-agent,"New model file passed 2/2, including all 500 random GitHub label sets executed through prepared importer mutations and SDK read-back. It covers commas, case, spaces, normalized duplicates, Unicode, prefixes, prototype-like names, raw older-plan replay, refresh no-op/delta agreement, JSON/TOON validation, unresolved choices and stale revisions. Reverting only the planner source conversion also makes this property fail at its first mismatching source impact (exit 1), then byte-identical restoration passes the CSV regression. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and duplication pass; 24 authored modules have zero duplicated lines. Public read-only non-git snapshot f90f86f has 155 items, 12 labels, one affected stored item/tag and two declared example policies, 3 rows and 1146 JSON bytes, source unchanged. The first packed install attempt timed out before consumer assertions; retry disables optional npm audit/funding requests, with deadlines and acceptance assertions unchanged. Full release gates remain CI evidence."
  "2026-10-27T12:26:50.764Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance exposed an additional producer/validator agreement gap: host TOON omits null terminal fields, although JSON and the SDK report retain them. The shared strict output schema now declares null defaults for a completed continuation and nullable policy fields; consumers parse both JSON and decoded TOON through that one validator. Tag and mapping identities remain required, unfinished pages still require the exact continuation, and malformed expansions still refuse. The packed assertions are strengthened to compare complete validated reports for both formats, rather than counts alone. Added must-allow compact-null records and must-refuse incomplete pagination and missing/null tag identities. This changes no tag conversion or SDK state logic. Native Bun class regressions pass 2/2; the pinned-pm linked CSV regression passed, with result tracking disabled by existing project policy."
  "2026-10-27T13:03:07.872Z",codex-agent,"Completed the host-wire class through public SDK encodePmTableRows/decodePmTableRows, not a second JSON-cell decoder. Strict canonical row schemas derive the accepted table field names; metadata validates dense bounded arrays, finite integer coordinates, unique columns/coordinates and null padding, then SDK restoration is checked against the same producer schema. The 500 SDK table permutations pass for all row kinds, sparse fields and JSON-looking strings; invalid JSON, unsafe numbers and malformed metadata refuse with invalid_output. Five independent reversions (SDK restoration, terminal null, filter nulls, mapping nulls, negative-coordinate guard) each fail their regression, then restore byte-for-byte. Final focused planner/wire tests pass 12/12 with 100/100/100/100 targeted coverage of labels.ts and import-tags.ts; the earlier complete feature file passed 12/12 including the existing 500 SDK state sequences. New importer model passed 2/2 with 500 random label sets. Installation setup alone now allows 600 seconds due observed host/registry timeouts; runtime command deadlines remain 180 seconds, assertions/pins/release thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T13:20:56.856Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passed all five actual install modes on CLI 2026.10.26 and Bun 1.3.14: project-local, npx, bunx, npm-global and Bun-global. Every mode compares complete canonical reports in JSON and TOON, revalidates current approval, refuses unresolved CSV tag choices and retains byte-identical non-git public tracker data. Measurements remain 155 items, 12 labels, one affected item/tag plus one declared filter and one mapping, 3 rows and 1146 JSON bytes at f90f86f. Additional standalone API checks loaded the installed artifact with SDK 2026.10.26 under both Node and Bun, previewed the same 155-item copy and restored SDK table output through the package validator; both passed. Native Bun current CSV/wire tests passed 2/2 including 500 wire permutations. Pinned-pm linked CSV and wire runs each passed 1/1; tracking remains disabled by existing policy. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, docstrings and duplication pass; 24 authored modules have zero duplicated lines. Full npm/Bun gate URLs and exact final counts will be maintained in PR 188; earlier-head or canceled runs are not current full-gate evidence. No further code findings remain from the supplied reviews or class audit."
